        "id": 3314159
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T12:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s correct. Since on Intel we can\u0027t offline the core 0, we can\u0027t offline P-cores. So the next best thing is to let them go into the deepest possible power-saving state and stay there without interruptions.\n\nAs for when it might happen: in use-cases where we know we won\u0027t need power cores. E.g. full-screen video playback. As for what could trigger it - combination of IPower HAL and vendor services.",
      "parentUuid": "e1bacb76_48a98189",
      "revId": "586352d88170cd89f6d40f08fc6c7e848eaa6bfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
